-- title:
--   Residues of the affine chart generate Fₛₛ, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`). Let $W$ be a finset of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)(M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ q\ M'$, let $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$, and let $s\in W$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$ and algebraically closed residue field, and such that every $a\in A$ is congruent to some element of $k_0\cap A$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $K_b$ be the trivial intermediate field $\bot$ of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_b$ the valuation subring of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, assumed a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by a nonzero $\varpi_b$. Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ and valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is everything, $x\in A \iff x\in W_0$ for $x\in k_0$, $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and the image of $\pi_0$ generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$; for every subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ on $A_b\subseteq K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with $B\subseteq W_0$ and $W_0=\{g/h: g,h\in B,\ \varpi_b\nmid h\}$; and for every field $F_{ss}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ with residue field $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing the inclusion of $A$ and its residue field, and with every nonzero $f$ scalable into $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue) such that $R.\mathrm{integers}\cap F_0=W_0$ and $B\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$: every $x\in F_{ss}$ can be written as $x=\bar g/\bar h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\bar h\neq 0$, and for $b\in B$ one has $\bar b=0$ if and only if $\varpi_b$ divides $b$ in $B$.
--
--   This identifies the residue field $F_{ss}$ of a regular prolongation of $A$ at a supersingular place as the fraction field of $B/\varpi_b B$: the residues of the affine chart $B$ generate $F_{ss}$, and the kernel of reduction on $B$ is exactly $\varpi_b B$. It is the $q=3$ case, on the Igusa-tower branch of the semistable specialisation of the full-level modular curve, of the corresponding statement for larger $q$, and feeds the construction of the supersingular discrete valuation rings and base smooth point stalks used there.
